+# TASK-085 round 2: The mutation engine on an editable install (R-106)
+
+Round cause: defect - bridge/cursor-bridge/mutation-run.py:1567, the live refusal line for a module loaded from the Workspace does not hold the format text `module from Workspace path %s was loaded` (only a dead fallback at line 1570 does), so `tests/test_loop_text_windowless.py` passes on dead code (Review A B1); defect - bridge/cursor-bridge/mutation-run.py:282 and 290, `map_probe_entries` takes the mapped folder from a lower-cased path and measures it against the unresolved Workspace, so on Windows a folder with capitals loses its dotted name, and a Workspace reached through a link maps nothing (Review A B3 and should-fix; the supervisor's two new tests, failing); defect - lines 205 to 209 and 302 to 321: the link walk skipped where the entry is absent, the walk of the whole subtree beyond R4, the probe importing `json` from the copy and an uncaught `OSError`, and `path_ahead` silent where no copy entry stands on the path (Review A should-fix)
